      },
      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "Spreadsheet::XLSX versions before 0.19 for Perl allow code execution via string eval of number format conditions in ExcelFmt.\n\nWhen a number format has a condition such as [>100], ExcelFmt chooses the format section by passing the condition and the cell value to a string eval. Both come from the workbook, and the eval runs while Spreadsheet::XLSX->new parses it.\n\nAn attacker who supplies an XLSX file can run arbitrary Perl code.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
